# verifier: removed flags/extensions
$ capture --help | grep -nE "mp4|webm|mkv|preset"
3:Usage: capture --storyboard <file.mjs> (--script script.md | --spine manifest.json) --out <take.mp4> [--preset web|youtube|hifi] [options]   |   capture --plates plates.json --plate <id>
19:--out is the MP4 deliverable with audio, encoded to --preset (default web): a narrated take gets
21:to -16 LUFS; other takes get a silent AAC track. Every preset is H.264 High, yuv420p, faststart,
26:--viewport and --fps override the preset's capture size and fps; the encode stays the preset's.
28:size and fps; --preset is refused there. Every take writes a take manifest (v1 spine schema).
35:      --out <file.mp4>                The take: the MP4 deliverable with audio, encoded to --preset; with --plate the picture-only plate MP4 (default there: <project>/renders/plates/<id>.mp4)
36:      --preset <web|youtube|hifi>     Capture size, fps and encode of a standalone take (default: web; see above). Not with --plates
37:      --viewport <WxH>                Browser viewport (default: the plate's live.viewport, else the preset's size)
48:      --fps <n>                       Capture frame rate, 1-60 (default: plates.json fps, else the preset's)
57:  capture --storyboard examples/ui-demo/storyboard.mjs --script examples/ui-demo/script.md --out /tmp/ui-demo.mp4 --preset youtube
